# The demo uses every feature, as a monitor would

Read `docs/demo.md` before editing `cmd/demo/**` or the public API in `pkg/webui/**`.

- The demo is **Collector**, a mock device-monitoring app. Every page belongs to it. No page exists only to show a feature, and none is named for a layout, a loading case or a feature.
- A new or changed public name, field or option of `pkg/webui` is used in a page of the demo where a monitor would need it, in that page's words. If it has no sensible use there, list it in `docs/demo.md` under "Not used, and why", with the reason. Do not invent a use for it.
- Update the table in `docs/demo.md` in the same change.
- The landing page (`/`) is the plain one: ordinary panels, ordinary layout, no edge cases. It is what the README shows.
- Keep page paths (the browser suite and `TestEveryPageServes` read them) and what a page's tests prove. Add no check that fails on an unused name.
